course: dictionary
lesson: 5327
title: One food, many names
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Ketchup is a noun, and it is uncountable, so you say «some ketchup» or «a squirt of ketchup», not «two ketchups». The sentences around a word tell you how it is used.
explain: «In Glasgow, Kyle says «gimme the ketchup» at a mate's house.» He asks for it at a meal, so it is something you pass across the table to eat with your food.
explain: Different countries have different names for the same thing. The full name is «tomato ketchup», and in the US it is sometimes spelled «catsup». In Australia and New Zealand people often say «tomato sauce». When you meet a new name, check the context and the dictionary.
fact: Ketchup is a noun, and it is uncountable.
fact: «Ketchup» means a thick red sauce made from tomatoes, vinegar, sugar and spices, eaten with chips, burgers and other food.
fact: The full name is «tomato ketchup», and in the US it is sometimes spelled «catsup».
fact: In Australia and New Zealand people often say «tomato sauce».
fact: Ketchup is a strange liquid: it gets runnier when you shake it, which is why hitting the bottle helps.
exercise: What is ketchup? | *A thick red sauce made from tomatoes, vinegar, sugar and spices | A clear, sweet drink made from lemons | A green vegetable like peas | A type of cheese made from milk
exercise: In Australia and New Zealand people often say «tomato sauce». What do they mean? | *Ketchup | A jam made from strawberries | A soup made from tomatoes | A pizza topping of cheese
exercise: What do people often eat ketchup with? | Soup in a bowl | Cereal with milk | *Chips and burgers | Ice cream on a cone
test: In the US, what is ketchup sometimes spelled? | *Catsup | Ketchop | Kechap | Cathup
test: Ketchup is uncountable. Which phrase is correct? | *some ketchup on my chips | three ketchup on my chips | two ketchups on my chips
exam: Which of these is the best description of ketchup? | A dry biscuit eaten at breakfast | A clear, sweet drink | A green leaf from a tree | *A thick red sauce made from tomatoes, vinegar, sugar and spices
